| ID | Raw neighbors / final decision | Expected as-built distinction and intended boundary |
|---|---|---|
| R1 | graph None, empty, named; same ID in multiple graphs; SQL NULL default | Every selected table scopes equally; None all, empty includes NULL/empty, named only matching graph. Source own-graph label EXISTS prevents bare-ID label crossover. |
| R2 | node_ids/label_filter omitted versus empty versus nonempty | Empty lists unfiltered; outgoing source IDs only; matching label rows only, selected subject's properties/edges use same-graph membership. Matching target alone does not admit edge. |
| R3 | no SQL node content vs label/property/edge subject | No nodes table scan; isolated node with no represented row contributes no RDF term/count. Subject count can exclude endpoints with no outgoing content. |
| R4 | two unqualified physical parallel rows | Base SPO set insertion collapses them per context/union; count is not physical row count. |
| R5 | same SPO in two graph contexts | Serialized NQ can have2quads versus report1union triple; preserve this as-built reader distinction without deciding broader counts-what-written policy. |
| R6 | one/two qualified parallel rows | Each qualified physical row gets2fresh blankterms; disjoint envelopes survive despite duplicate base SPO. Allocation derives from row positions, not supplied unique IDs. |
| R7 | empty/nonempty/inferred-only qualifier object | Nonempty original dict creates4envelope triples before inferred key omission; inferred-only still has envelope. |
| R8 | property false/0 versus qualifier false/0 | Property literal is typed; qualifier `_to_literal(str(qv)) or Literal(str(qv))` yields plain false/zero due literal truthiness. As-built, no policy answer/defect inferred from broad guide alone. |
| R9 | canonical integer, leading-zero numeric text, admitted exact-dyadic text, true/false, ordinary/empty text | Parse order and canonical integer check derive datatype. No supplied datatype flags; arbitrary float/native/normalization remains conditional. |
| R10 | bare ID versus http/https/urn/ftp; property key ftp | Node mint preserves all4prefixes; property passthrough preserves http/https/urn only. Keep exact distinction or explicit supported-key fragment. |
| R11 | named canonical ASCII graph versus default | Context comes from raw row graph; graph_iri broader absolute-IRI/percent encoding is a conditional codec boundary unless modeled. No Universal Unicode law. |
| R12 | summary triples/subjects/edges vs physical rows/nodes/endpoints | Derive union cardinalities; exclude rdf:type for URI-object edge count; include blank subjects and reification URI-object triples. Actual final serialized parse remains a separate reader. |
| R13 | SQL/namespace/serialize failure versus successful empty | Preserve actual stage outcomes when claimed; successful empty not substituted for errors. No independent native/transaction/whole-format proof. |

No new proof/family/shared/source/Git/native/network changes in this freeze. No fixed stopping cap, private grade, population rate or convergence claim.
